      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:53:3",
      "text": [
        " إِذَا كُنْتَ خَلْفَ إِمَامٍ تَأْتَمُّ بِهِ فَأَنْصِتْ وَ سَبِّحْ فِي نَفْسِكَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali, from his father, from Hammad, from Hareyz, from Zurara, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from one of the two (5<sup>th</sup> or 6<sup>th</sup> Imam<sup>asws</sup>) having said: ‘When you were to be behind a Imam, complete with him, and be silent (during the recitation), and Glorify within yourself’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali has narrated from his father from Hammad from Hariz from Zurarah who has said the following: “One of the two Imam, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If you perform Salah (prayer) behind an Imam whom you follow then remain silent and say Tasbih (Allah is free of all defects) to yourself only.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
